            <button x="250" y="55" width="183" height="30" uid="22" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Intro: Build Your Own Model!" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-184" y="40" width="617" height="346" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">If you haven&apos;t modeled before, watch our Build Your Own Personal Finance Model video to help you get started with using STELLA modeling software, available at http://clexchange.org/curriculum/dollarsandsense.asp &#x0D;&#x0D;Choose from 3 options:&#x0D;&#x0D;(1) Use this blank STELLA page to build your own model from scratch. Everything you need is here (icons/buttons for building blocks, tables and graphs, text; Word menus to run and print...);  OR&#x0D;&#x0D;(2) Click on the &quot;Explore Simple Stock and Flow Model&quot; button to see the core pre-built stock and flow model (Go ahead and make changes -- insert new numbers, change names, add building blocks!);  OR&#x0D;&#x0D;(3) Click on the &quot;Explore Model Used in Lesson 1&quot; to explore a version of the actual model used in Lesson 1 (it&apos;s a bit more complicated, but everything in it is explained!). &#x0D;&#x0D;&#x0D;Start wherever you want! And have fun!&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <button x="485" y="545" width="146" height="31" uid="23" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Model Used in Lesson 1" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="1176" />
            </button>
            <text_box x="4" y="1" uid="24" color="red" font-family="Comic Sans MS" font-size="32" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="756" height="55">Can I Manage My Money and My Music?</text_box>
            <button x="282" y="651" width="129" height="34" uid="25" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="What can I do with this?" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-116" y="285" width="367" height="187" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">Here&apos;s a very simple version of the Stock and Flow model used in Lesson 1. &quot;Monthly Deposits&quot; effect the rate that $$ flow into MY SAVINGS. &quot;Monthly Expenses&quot; effect the rate that $$ flow out. &#x0D;&#x0D;Explore (e.g., change amounts ($) for deposits or expenses; rename or add new building blocks to make this your model). Play with it and have fun!!&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <button x="267" y="991" width="65" height="34" uid="26" appearance="opaque" background="#7F00FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Run" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <menu_action>run</menu_action>
            </button>
            <button x="323" y="545" width="146" height="31" uid="27" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Simple Stock and Flow Model" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="588" />
            </button>
            <button x="162" y="545" width="147" height="32" uid="28" appearance="opaque" background="#E0E0E0" color="white" style="square" label="Build Your Own Model " font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="0" />
            </button>
            <button x="441" y="1137" width="146" height="31" uid="29" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Model Used in Lesson 1" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="1176" />
            </button>
            <button x="279" y="1137" width="146" height="31" uid="30" appearance="opaque" background="#E0E0E0" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Simple Stock and Flow Model" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="588" />
            </button>
            <button x="118" y="1137" width="147" height="32" uid="31" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Build Your Own Model " font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="0" />
            </button>
            <button x="439" y="1719" width="146" height="31" uid="32" appearance="opaque" background="#E0E0E0" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Model Used in Lesson 1" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="1176" />
            </button>
            <button x="277" y="1719" width="146" height="31" uid="33" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Simple Stock and Flow Model" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="588" />
            </button>
            <button x="116" y="1719" width="147" height="32" uid="34" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Build Your Own Model " font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="0" />
            </button>
            <button x="282" y="1238" width="129" height="34" uid="35" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="What can I do with this?" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-276" y="-11" width="284" height="489" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">This is a version of the model underlying the Lesson 1 Simulation. When you click and open any building block, you will find an explanation for how it works.&#x0D;&#x0D;Remember, this model does NOT allow you to make any purchases UNTIL you reach your Personal Savings Goal. That is why there are additional building blocks recording when you REACH (your personal savings) GOAL. &#x0D;&#x0D;Explore how you can make changes (e.g., change numbers; rename or add new building blocks to make this your model). Play with it and have fun!&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <text_box x="12" y="594" uid="36" color="red" font-family="Comic Sans MS" font-size="32" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="746" height="56">Simple Stock/Flow Model (used in Lesson 1) </text_box>
            <text_box x="11" y="1179" uid="37" color="red" font-family="Comic Sans MS" font-size="32" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="746" height="56"> Model Used in Lesson 1</text_box>
            <button x="344" y="992" width="65" height="34" uid="38" appearance="opaque" background="#7F00FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Reset" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <menu_action>restore_all</menu_action>
            </button>
            <button x="573" y="1654" width="65" height="34" uid="39" appearance="opaque" background="#7F00FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Run" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <menu_action>run</menu_action>
